<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
    <version>3.5.16</version>
    <relativePath/>
  </parent>

  <groupId>com.flowops</groupId>
  <artifactId>flowops</artifactId>
  <version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
  <name>flowops</name>
  <description>FlowOps backend</description>

  <properties>
    <java.version>21</java.version>
    <archunit.version>1.4.2</archunit.version>
    <jacoco.version>0.8.13</jacoco.version>
    <spotless.version>2.44.5</spotless.version>
    <palantir.version>2.50.0</palantir.version>
    <checkstyle.plugin.version>3.6.0</checkstyle.plugin.version>
    <checkstyle.version>10.26.1</checkstyle.version>
    <dependency.check.version>12.2.2</dependency.check.version>
    <springdoc.version>2.8.17</springdoc.version>
    <swagger.ui.version>5.32.11</swagger.ui.version>

    <!--
      **The default runs everything, and `-P fast` is what skips.** Inverted on 2026-08-22, after
      the previous arrangement — skip `roundtrip` unless `-P full` is named — hid a production
      defect for a whole slice.

      What it hid: `V55` dropped `step_definition.title`, and `TemplateHistoryAdapter` was still
      querying it, so `GET /api/insights` answered **500 to every caller**. The ordinary build
      reported *1063 tests, BUILD SUCCESS* throughout, because the suite that reaches that
      endpoint carries the `roundtrip` tag. The count was true and covered nothing that mattered.

      The old comment here advised reading `target/surefire-reports` rather than the console
      summary, which is correct and is not a control: it asks every reader to remember a caveat in
      order to avoid a trap, and the reader who most needs it is the one who has forgotten. A
      default that runs everything needs nothing remembered. The inner loop pays for it, and the
      inner loop is where a slow run is noticed and worked around rather than silently trusted.

      `architecture` is not skipped by either setting. The tag marks the four tests that need a
      Spring context, not the rules about package boundaries — `ArchitectureRulesTest` carries no
      tag and runs regardless. Two of the four are `PermissionsAreSeededTest` and
      `EveryEnforcedPermissionReachesARoleTest`, which catch a permission declared and granted to
      nobody: the failure `V42`'s comment records, where every endpoint answers 403 to everyone
      including the owner while the whole unit suite stays green.

      A property rather than an `activeByDefault` profile because Maven deactivates default
      profiles the moment any other profile is named, and a build that silently changes what it
      runs is the whole problem being fixed here.

      `livemodel` is excluded even from the full run, and it is the one exclusion that is about the
      machine rather than about speed. Those tests call a language model over HTTP on localhost:
      without `docker compose up -d ollama` they fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the
      code, and a suite that goes red when a container is not running teaches people to ignore red.

      They are measurements rather than guarantees. Run them deliberately:
        ./mvnw test -Dtest=TheModelAnswersAndStaysInertTest -Ddemo.excluded.test.groups=
    -->
    <demo.excluded.test.groups>livemodel</demo.excluded.test.groups>

    <!--
      Ahead of what the Spring Boot bill of materials pins. Each carries a fix for an
      advisory the dependency scan flags; drop the override once the bill of materials
      catches up, which the scan will confirm.
    -->
    <tomcat.version>10.1.57</tomcat.version>
    <postgresql.version>42.7.13</postgresql.version>
    <log4j2.version>2.26.1</log4j2.version>
    <javadoc.plugin.version>3.12.0</javadoc.plugin.version>
  </properties>

  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-jpa</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-security</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-validation</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <!-- Delivers the signup passcode to the local catcher (DECISION-MAIL-CATCHER-01). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-mail</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.session</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-session-jdbc</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The HTTP contract is published from the code as OpenAPI (CONSTRAINT-API-FIRST-01). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>
      <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</artifactId>
      <version>${springdoc.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- Declared directly so the bundled browser assets can be moved ahead of the
         version springdoc pins, which carries known advisories. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.webjars</groupId>
      <artifactId>swagger-ui</artifactId>
      <version>${swagger.ui.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
      <artifactId>flyway-core</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
      <artifactId>flyway-database-postgresql</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
      <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
      <scope>runtime</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-devtools</artifactId>
      <scope>runtime</scope>
      <optional>true</optional>
    </dependency>

    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-security-test</artifactId>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-testcontainers</artifactId>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
      <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
      <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.tngtech.archunit</groupId>
      <artifactId>archunit</artifactId>
      <version>${archunit.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
      </plugin>

      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <excludedGroups>${demo.excluded.test.groups}</excludedGroups>
          <systemPropertyVariables>
            <!--
              Docker Engine 29 refuses API versions below 1.40, and the Docker client bundled
              with Testcontainers negotiates lower than that, so every container request comes
              back as an empty 400. Pinning the version keeps Testcontainers working without
              per-machine configuration.
            -->
            <api.version>1.44</api.version>
          </systemPropertyVariables>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>

      <plugin>
        <groupId>com.diffplug.spotless</groupId>
        <artifactId>spotless-maven-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${spotless.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <java>
            <palantirJavaFormat>
              <version>${palantir.version}</version>
            </palantirJavaFormat>
            <removeUnusedImports/>
            <trimTrailingWhitespace/>
            <endWithNewline/>
          </java>
          <pom>
            <sortPom>
              <expandEmptyElements>false</expandEmptyElements>
            </sortPom>
          </pom>
        </configuration>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <goals>
              <goal>check</goal>
            </goals>
            <phase>validate</phase>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>

      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-checkstyle-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${checkstyle.plugin.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <configLocation>${project.basedir}/checkstyle.xml</configLocation>
          <includeTestSourceDirectory>true</includeTestSourceDirectory>
          <consoleOutput>true</consoleOutput>
          <failsOnError>true</failsOnError>
          <violationSeverity>warning</violationSeverity>
        </configuration>
        <dependencies>
          <dependency>
            <groupId>com.puppycrawl.tools</groupId>
            <artifactId>checkstyle</artifactId>
            <version>${checkstyle.version}</version>
          </dependency>
        </dependencies>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <id>verify-style</id>
            <goals>
              <goal>check</goal>
            </goals>
            <phase>validate</phase>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>

      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-javadoc-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${javadoc.plugin.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <doclint>all,-missing</doclint>
          <quiet>true</quiet>
        </configuration>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <id>generate-javadoc</id>
            <goals>
              <goal>jar</goal>
            </goals>
            <phase>package</phase>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>

      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.jacoco</groupId>
        <artifactId>jacoco-maven-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${jacoco.version}</version>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <id>prepare-agent</id>
            <goals>
              <goal>prepare-agent</goal>
            </goals>
          </execution>
          <execution>
            <id>report</id>
            <goals>
              <goal>report</goal>
            </goals>
            <phase>verify</phase>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>

      <!-- Invoked explicitly by CI; not bound to a phase so local builds stay fast. -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.owasp</groupId>
        <artifactId>dependency-check-maven</artifactId>
        <version>${dependency.check.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <failBuildOnCVSS>7</failBuildOnCVSS>
          <!--
            Without this, the check also fails on advisories the national database has
            not scored yet. That makes the gate non-deterministic: a newly published,
            unassessed advisory breaks the build overnight with nothing to judge it by.
            The gate is a severity threshold, so it fails on severity.
          -->
          <failOnUnscored>false</failOnUnscored>
          <!--
            Sonatype's index answers 401 without an account, so every request failed and
            the accumulated failures failed the build. It never returned a single result.
            It was also the source of mis-parsed severity scores, which made the check
            reject advisories scoring below the threshold. The national vulnerability
            database remains the source, and it needs no account.
          -->
          <ossindexAnalyzerEnabled>false</ossindexAnalyzerEnabled>
          <nvdApiKey>${env.NVD_API_KEY}</nvdApiKey>
          <formats>
            <format>HTML</format>
            <format>JSON</format>
          </formats>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>

  <profiles>
    <!--
      The inner loop: everything except the forty-six round trips, each of which starts Tomcat
      against a real PostgreSQL container. `./mvnw -P fast test` while iterating on a domain rule.

      **It is never the profile a claim is made from.** A count produced here has not touched an
      endpoint, a migration or a permission grant, and saying "the suite passes" on the strength of
      it is the reading that hid a 500 for a slice (`IMPL-SOP-PROFILE`).
    -->
    <profile>
      <id>fast</id>
      <properties>
        <demo.excluded.test.groups>roundtrip,livemodel</demo.excluded.test.groups>
      </properties>
    </profile>

    <!--
      Kept so that `-P full` still means what it meant, rather than failing as an unknown profile
      in a script, a runbook or somebody's shell history. It now selects the default, which is the
      point: the two names agree instead of one of them being a trap.
    -->
    <profile>
      <id>full</id>
      <properties>
        <demo.excluded.test.groups>livemodel</demo.excluded.test.groups>
      </properties>
    </profile>
  </profiles>

</project>
